  "slug": "high-nanoantenna-b3b2",
  "summary": "Recent preprints report active tuning of quasi-BIC resonances, excitonic strong coupling in bulk WS2, and strain-driven terahertz modulation in crystals.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is controlling resonant response in nanophotonic structures through mode coupling and the surrounding environment. Two items address quasi-bound states in the continuum: a symmetric silicon metasurface embedded in a nematic liquid crystal, whose anisotropy-induced quasi-BICs are actively tunable, and bulk WS2 metasurfaces in which Brillouin-zone-folding quasi-BICs self-hybridize with A excitons into polarization-independent strong coupling. A review of terahertz phase modulation via strain in piezoelectric and nonlinear optical crystals addresses a related goal of dynamic control through a different physical route. The MXene-derived TiO2 polarizer on silicon photonics is a device-level result that sits at the edge of this thread. What is new is active spectral control via liquid-crystal integration and excitonic strong coupling in bulk material. All four items are preprints.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
